// @probe reject: the rest was not read
// The mini-parser inside `${...}` stopped at the first thing it could not continue and nothing
// looked at the remainder, so `$"{a >= 1 and a <= 2}"` printed the value of `a >= 1`. With a = 5
// that is `true`, where the whole condition is false: a plausible wrong value, in silence, in
// the construct the language is most used through.
agent Main { public void Run() { var a = 5; print $"{a >= 1 and a <= 2}"; } }
